Package: InfoMergeCluster
Type: Package
Title: Clustering of Sparse Longitudinal Data with Automatic Selection of the Number of Clusters
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = c("Komlan", "Midodzi"),
           family = "Noukpoape",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "noukpoape@gmail.com")
Description: Model-based clustering of sparse and irregular longitudinal
    data. Each cluster has a penalized B-spline mean trajectory (O'Sullivan
    penalty with an automatically estimated smoothing parameter) and
    subject-specific deviations are captured by a random effect (intercept,
    linear or spline). Conjugate priors calibrated on the empirical variogram
    of the residuals stabilize the variance components. The EM algorithm,
    accelerated by SQUAREM, works on subject-level sufficient statistics and
    is initialized by a merge tree of micro-clusters based on the exact
    integrated completed likelihood. The number of clusters is selected by
    BIC or ICL, or can be imposed by the user. Tools are provided for
    confidence and prediction envelopes, predicted individual trajectories
    and stability across random seeds.
